course: dictionary
lesson: 775
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word beat has several meanings, so context tells you which one to use. Read the words around it first. Beat can mean win, hit again and again, mix fast, a regular sound, or very tired.
explain: «At the chess tournament Dev from another school beats Sam on time in the final.» The clues are chess, final and on time, so beats means wins. Would hitting fit here? No, so winning is the right meaning.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense. Dev wins against Sam makes sense in the chess sentence, so you have found the meaning.
fact: Beat is one word with several meanings, so always check the context.
fact: As a verb, beat can mean to win against someone, to hit again and again, or to mix food fast, like eggs.
fact: As a noun, a beat is a regular sound or pulse, like the beat of a drum or a heart.
fact: Informally, beat means very tired, as in «I am beat after the match».
fact: «Beat it» means go away.
exercise: «At the chess tournament Dev from another school beats Sam on time in the final.» What does beats mean here? | Makes a regular sound | Hits Sam again and again | Mixes Sam quickly | *Wins against Sam
exercise: In «In 3/4 time each bar holds three crotchet beats», what is a beat? | A type of wheat | A hit with a stick | A kind of bread | *A regular pulse, like a drum
exercise: Ella says, «I am beat after the long walk!» What does beat mean? | Mixed fast | *Very tired | Hit again and again | Won a race
test: To beat eggs in a bowl means to | Crack them open with a hammer | Cook them slowly | *Mix them fast | Count them
test: What does «beat it» mean? | Count the beats | Mix it fast | Win the game | *Go away
exam: Which sentence uses beat to mean hit again and again? | *The rain beat on the window all night. | Dev beats Sam in the final. | I am beat after the match. | The beat of the drum is steady.
